            Standard tuning.
Fun 4 chord song, intermediate only for the voicings, but if you got bar chords down, it should be easy.
Play A F#m and D as bar chords, E open.
Rhythm is down, up-down-up-down, up-down-up-down, up for each chord during the breaks ("elephants and
zebras," "be with you always," etc.) and Chorus ("and it de-fi-NIT-ly matters...").
Verse, bridge, and coda are just downstrokes, with palm-muting...
...or play it how like.  Have fun!

